IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P4-gate`

-- P4-art-33-35: Article 33 (Subsidiaries of notified bodies and subcontracting), Article 34 (Operational obligations of notified bodies),
-- Article 35 (Identification numbers and lists of notified bodies). None was changed by the Omnibus (marker `▼B`): one text, both versions.
-- Every function takes `the date asked` first and answers NOTHING before Chapter III Section 4 applies (2 August 2025).

§ `Articles 33 to 35: the parties and acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `Art 33 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 33 notified body`

DECLARE `Art 33 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 33(1) ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31`
    `Art 33(1) inform the notifying authority of the subcontracting or the recourse to a subsidiary`
    `Art 33(3) make a list of its subsidiaries publicly available`

DECLARE `Art 34 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 34 notified body`

DECLARE `Art 34 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 34(1) verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43`
    `Art 34(3) make available and submit upon request all relevant documentation to the notifying authority`

DECLARE `Art 35 party` IS ONE OF
    `Art 35 Commission`

DECLARE `Art 35 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 35(1) assign a single identification number to each notified body`
    `Art 35(2) make publicly available the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation`
    `Art 35(2) keep the list up to date`

§ `Article 33(1): subcontracting and subsidiaries`

-- src:586 | 1. Where a notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary, it shall ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, and shall inform the notifying authority accordingly.
@ref Art 33(1) (src:586)
-- Gloss: where a notified body hands specific tasks to a subcontractor or a subsidiary, it makes sure that body meets Article 31 and tells the notifying authority.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has ensured that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has informed the notifying authority accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(1) the notified body has ensured the requirements are met and informed the notifying authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a notified body subcontracts specific tasks ... or has recourse to a subsidiary" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST (   `the notified body has ensured that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31`
                   AND `the notified body has informed the notifying authority accordingly`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, and shall inform the notifying authority accordingly" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show these rules breached.
-- src:586 | 1. Where a notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary, it shall ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, and shall inform the notifying authority accordingly.
@ref Art 33(1) (src:586)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 33 party` `Art 33 act`
`Art 33(1) the duty of the notified body to ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 33 notified body`
         MUST `Art 33(1) ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31`
         HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:586 | 1. Where a notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary, it shall ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, and shall inform the notifying authority accordingly.
@ref Art 33(1) (src:586)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 33 party` `Art 33 act`
`Art 33(1) the duty of the notified body to inform the notifying authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 33 notified body`
         MUST `Art 33(1) inform the notifying authority of the subcontracting or the recourse to a subsidiary`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 33(2): full responsibility`

-- src:587 | 2. Notified bodies shall take full responsibility for the tasks performed by any subcontractors or subsidiaries.
@ref Art 33(2) (src:587)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body takes full responsibility for the tasks performed by any subcontractors or subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(2) the notified body takes full responsibility for the tasks performed by subcontractors and subsidiaries` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notified body takes full responsibility for the tasks performed by any subcontractors or subsidiaries`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall take full responsibility for the tasks performed by any subcontractors or subsidiaries" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 33(3): the provider's agreement, and the list of subsidiaries`

-- src:588 | 3. Activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary only with the agreement of the provider. Notified bodies shall make a list of their subsidiaries publicly available.
@ref Art 33(3) (src:588)
-- Gloss: work may be subcontracted or done by a subsidiary only if the provider agrees; and the notified body publishes a list of its subsidiaries.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the provider has agreed to the activities being subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(3) first sentence the activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the provider has agreed to the activities being subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary only with the agreement of the provider" (a list closed with "only")

-- src:588 | 3. Activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary only with the agreement of the provider. Notified bodies shall make a list of their subsidiaries publicly available.
@ref Art 33(3) (src:588)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has made a list of its subsidiaries publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(3) second sentence the notified body has made the list of its subsidiaries publicly available` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notified body has made a list of its subsidiaries publicly available`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall make a list of their subsidiaries publicly available" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:588 | 3. Activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary only with the agreement of the provider. Notified bodies shall make a list of their subsidiaries publicly available.
@ref Art 33(3) (src:588)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 33 party` `Art 33 act`
`Art 33(3) the duty of the notified body to make a list of its subsidiaries publicly available` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
