         MUST `Art 33(3) make a list of its subsidiaries publicly available`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 33(4): keeping the documents for five years`

-- The period of five years runs from the termination date of the subcontracting. The text does not say how a year is counted: the same day five years on,
-- the last day of the month where there is none (`add years`; fork F-months).
-- src:589 | 4. The relevant documents concerning the assessment of the qualifications of the subcontractor or the subsidiary and the work carried out by them under this Regulation shall be kept at the disposal of the notifying authority for a period of five years from the termination date of the subcontracting.
@ref Art 33(4) (src:589)
-- Gloss: the papers on how the subcontractor or subsidiary was assessed and what it did stay available to the notifying authority for five years after the subcontracting ends. The text does not say who must keep them (fork F-passive), so there is no regulative rule for it.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the termination date of the subcontracting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(4) the five years from the termination date of the subcontracting are running` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF `the date asked` LESS THAN `the termination date of the subcontracting`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period runs "from the termination date"; the paragraph says nothing of the time before it
         ELSE JUST (`the date asked` AT MOST (`add years` `the termination date of the subcontracting` 5))  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of five years from the termination date of the subcontracting" (a period the text fixes: outside it, no)

-- src:589 | 4. The relevant documents concerning the assessment of the qualifications of the subcontractor or the subsidiary and the work carried out by them under this Regulation shall be kept at the disposal of the notifying authority for a period of five years from the termination date of the subcontracting.
@ref Art 33(4) (src:589)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the termination date of the subcontracting` IS A DATE
      `the relevant documents concerning the assessment of the qualifications of the subcontractor or the subsidiary and the work carried out by them under this Regulation are kept at the disposal of the notifying authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 33(4) the notified body has kept the documents at the disposal of the notifying authority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 33(4) the five years from the termination date of the subcontracting are running` `the date asked` `the termination date of the subcontracting`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group does not apply, or the period has not begun
    WHEN JUST `running` THEN
        IF `running`
        THEN JUST `the relevant documents concerning the assessment of the qualifications of the subcontractor or the subsidiary and the work carried out by them under this Regulation are kept at the disposal of the notifying authority`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be kept at the disposal of the notifying authority for a period of five years" (a bare "shall" not done)
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the five years have ended and the text states no duty after them

§ `Article 34(1): verifying conformity under Article 43`

-- src:592 | 1. Notified bodies shall verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43.
@ref Art 34(1) (src:592)
-- Gloss: the notified body checks the conformity of high-risk AI systems by the procedures of Article 43. Article 43 is another part's: its answer is taken as an input (seam S-43).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body has verified the conformity of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 34(1) the notified body has verified the conformity of the high-risk AI system` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notified body has verified the conformity of the high-risk AI system in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:592 | 1. Notified bodies shall verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43.
@ref Art 34(1) (src:592)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 34 party` `Art 34 act`
`Art 34(1) the duty of the notified body to verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 34 notified body`
         MUST `Art 34(1) verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 34(2): no unnecessary burdens, and no loss of rigour`

-- src:593 | 2. Notified bodies shall avoid unnecessary burdens for providers when performing their activities, and take due account of the size of the provider, the sector in which it operates, its structure and the degree of complexity of the high-risk AI system concerned, in particular in view of minimising administrative burdens and compliance costs for micro- and small enterprises within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC. The notified body shall, nevertheless, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required for the compliance of the high-risk AI system with the requirements of this Regulation.
@ref Art 34(2) (src:593)
-- Gloss: the notified body does not load providers with needless burdens, takes account of the provider's size, sector, structure and the system's complexity, and above all keeps the burden and cost low for micro and small enterprises; yet it does not relax the rigour or protection the Regulation requires.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body avoids unnecessary burdens for providers when performing its activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body takes due account of the size of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body takes due account of the sector in which the provider operates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body takes due account of the structure of the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body takes due account of the degree of complexity of the high-risk AI system concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a micro or small enterprise within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has minimised administrative burdens and compliance costs for that enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 34(2) first sentence the notified body has avoided unnecessary burdens and taken due account of the provider and the system` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the notified body avoids unnecessary burdens for providers when performing its activities`
        AND `the notified body takes due account of the size of the provider`
        AND `the notified body takes due account of the sector in which the provider operates`
        AND `the notified body takes due account of the structure of the provider`
        AND `the notified body takes due account of the degree of complexity of the high-risk AI system concerned`
        AND ((NOT `the provider is a micro or small enterprise within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC`) OR `the notified body has minimised administrative burdens and compliance costs for that enterprise`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notified bodies shall avoid unnecessary burdens for providers when performing their activities, and take due account of the size of the provider ... in particular in view of minimising administrative burdens and compliance costs for micro- and small enterprises" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- src:593 | 2. Notified bodies shall avoid unnecessary burdens for providers when performing their activities, and take due account of the size of the provider, the sector in which it operates, its structure and the degree of complexity of the high-risk AI system concerned, in particular in view of minimising administrative burdens and compliance costs for micro- and small enterprises within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC. The notified body shall, nevertheless, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required for the compliance of the high-risk AI system with the requirements of this Regulation.
@ref Art 34(2) (src:593)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notified body respects the degree of rigour and the level of protection required for the compliance of the high-risk AI system with the requirements of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 34(2) second sentence the notified body has respected the degree of rigour and the level of protection required` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the notified body respects the degree of rigour and the level of protection required for the compliance of the high-risk AI system with the requirements of this Regulation`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notified body shall, nevertheless, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required" (a bare "shall" not done)

§ `Article 34(3): documentation to the notifying authority on request`

