@ref Art 34(3) (src:594)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the notifying authority has requested the documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notified body has made available and submitted all relevant documentation, including the providers' documentation, to the notifying authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 34(3) the notified body has submitted the documentation upon request` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 4 applies from 2 August 2025
    ELSE IF NOT `the notifying authority has requested the documentation`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon request" (fork F-unmet-where)
         ELSE JUST `the notified body has made available and submitted all relevant documentation, including the providers' documentation, to the notifying authority`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall make available and submit upon request all relevant documentation" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
