§ `Article 35(1): a single identification number`

-- src:597 | 1. The Commission shall assign a single identification number to each notified body, even where a body is notified under more than one Union act.
@ref Art 35(1) (src:597)
-- Gloss: the Commission gives each notified body one number, even if it is notified under more than one Union act.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of identification numbers the Commission has assigned to the notified body` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 35(1) the Commission has assigned a single identification number to the notified body` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (`the number of identification numbers the Commission has assigned to the notified body` EQUALS 1)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall assign a single identification number to each notified body, even where a body is notified under more than one Union act" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show this rule breached.
-- src:597 | 1. The Commission shall assign a single identification number to each notified body, even where a body is notified under more than one Union act.
@ref Art 35(1) (src:597)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 35 party` `Art 35 act`
`Art 35(1) the duty of the Commission to assign a single identification number` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 28 to 39 the notified bodies group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed before Chapter III Section 4 applies
    ELSE PARTY `Art 35 Commission`
         MUST `Art 35(1) assign a single identification number to each notified body`
         HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 35(2): the public list`

-- src:598 | 2. The Commission shall make publicly available the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation, including their identification numbers and the activities for which they have been notified. The Commission shall ensure that the list is kept up to date.
@ref Art 35(2) (src:598)
-- Gloss: the Commission publishes the list of bodies notified under this Regulation, with their numbers and the activities they are notified for, and keeps it current.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission has made the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list includes the identification numbers of the bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list includes the activities for which the bodies have been notified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has kept the list up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 35(2) the Commission has made the list publicly available and kept it up to date` MEANS
    `Art 28 to 39 the answer when the group applies` `the date asked`
        (   `the Commission has made the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation publicly available`
        AND `the list includes the identification numbers of the bodies`
        AND `the list includes the activities for which the bodies have been notified`
        AND `the Commission has kept the list up to date`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall make publicly available the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation, including their identification numbers and the activities for which they have been notified. The Commission shall ensure that the list is kept up to date" (a bare "shall" not done)

-- No time limit and no consequence is stated, so no trace can show these rules breached.
